        "mission_intent": "Please develop a comprehensive specification for our Security Assessment Team Composition and Reporting Framework, aligned with NIST SP 800-115 guidance. We need a formal document that defines the required skill mix for assessment teams, ensuring balanced coverage across security domains rather than over-concentrating in any single specialty area such as perimeter defense. The spec should establish criteria for selecting team leaders based on overall technical knowledge, familiarity with the specific assessment techniques being employed, and understanding of the target assets under evaluation, along with demonstrated communication, organizational, planning, and conflict resolution competencies. Include requirements for embedding at least one team member with strong technical writing capability to ensure assessment results are effectively communicated to both technical and non-technical audiences, including senior leadership. The framework must address how the team leader facilitates coordination between assessors and the organization's security program management office, and define reporting templates that convey findings without jeopardizing organizational mission or damaging the credibility of the security program. Please incorporate role definitions, escalation paths, and quality review checkpoints for all deliverables. We'd like a draft ready for internal review by end of next quarter so we can pilot it during our fall assessment cycle.",
